      "path": "plugins/dsh-code-rag-index-panel/README.md",
      "content": "# dsh-code-rag-index-panel\n\n[中文文档](README.zh.md) | English\n\n**Code RAG index panel & settings card** for DeepSeek Harness — a live index status\nbar above the conversation input plus a diagnostics & configuration card in the\nsettings (Settings → **Plugins** on current DSH builds, and the legacy **Web Plugins**\nsection on older shells). Data flows through the companion\n[`@aylina_ankali/code-rag-mcp`](https://github.com/Ankali-Aylina/code-rag) MCP server\n(Qdrant vectors + Ollama `bge-m3` embeddings, Chinese/English queries both work).\n\n## Features\n\n**Index bar** (above the composer, `conversation.input.dock` slot):\n\n- Current root, index status, **live progress bar** (% / files / chunks), error details\n- Buttons: **Start index** (incremental) / **Full rebuild** / **Cancel**\n- Target root = **current session workspace** by default (any workspace can be indexed directly; falls back to the server root when the workspace is not a codebase)\n- Port discovery: probes 8756-8786 and picks the newest server (avoids stale instances)\n- All requests carry an 8s timeout — offline shows a hint instead of hanging forever\n- **Index bar scope switch** (v1.3.0): show it in **Code RAG mode sessions only** (default) or in **all sessions** — stored in DSH settings (`settings.yaml`, namespace `dsh-code-rag-index-panel`), takes effect immediately\n- **Bar appears as soon as you pick the mode** (v1.4.0): visibility keys off the session's agent preset (the dock subscribes to the session list, so it re-renders the moment the preset lands) instead of waiting for server-up timing. Select Code RAG mode without sending a message and the bar shows immediately with a \"starting the index server…\" hint — **it never auto-indexes** (start/rebuild buttons stay disabled until the server is ready, then you trigger them manually, so an accidental mode pick never burns local CPU/IO).\n- **Scope follows the session mode strictly** (v1.4.1): in strict mode (\"Code RAG mode sessions only\") the bar is shown **only** by the session's agent preset — the server's online state no longer matters. A code-rag server started by one Code RAG session keeps running while you switch to other-mode sessions; the old \"server-up fallback\" made the bar appear in every mode and has been removed. The \"all sessions\" mode behaves as before.\n\n**Settings card** (v1.4.0: both Settings → **Plugins** — the canonical plugin-card page, `settings.plugin.item` slot keyed by the namespace the host half registers via `settings.register` + schemastery — and Settings → **Web Plugins** → Code RAG, legacy `web-ui.plugin.item` compat slot; the new-plugins-page card degrades silently if the host half cannot register the namespace):\n\n| Endpoint (host half, loopback-only) | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `GET  /api/code-rag/diag` | One-click diagnostics: index server (port/pid/current root/per-root vector counts), Qdrant (reachable/collection), Ollama (reachable/model), mode preset (path/dist artifacts), config file — plus an **issue list** (including orphan-vector consistency checks) |\n| `POST /api/code-rag/config` | Write `<root>/.code-rag/config.json` (whitelisted keys, atomic write) |\n| `POST /api/code-rag/action` | `index` / `rebuild` / `cancel` (proxied to the index server) + `setup` (re-runs `scripts/setup.mjs` to regenerate the preset) |\n\nThe card offers: **Re-check** button, green/red status rows, issue list, config form\n(Qdrant/Ollama URLs, embedding model, dimensions, collection, port, chunk size,\nmulti-line **ignore rules**, configurable `root`), and index / rebuild / cancel /\nregenerate-preset actions. All file I/O is fault-tolerant; if the host endpoint is\nmissing the card shows a hint instead of failing. **Bilingual UI**: follows the\npage language (`<html lang>`) automatically — Chinese and English.\n\n**Stability fix** (v1.4.0): when the `settingsScope` namespace is unregistered or\nstill loading, `getSnapshot().value` is `undefined`; the old code read\n`.strictIndexBar` straight off it and threw a `TypeError`, which crashed the\nindex-bar/settings-card entries (slots retire crashed entries until the bundle\nreloads — this is what made the bar and card vanish). `undefined` is now treated\nas \"not set\" → strict default, and the namespace is registered with a real\nboolean schema so the value round-trips validated.\n\n## Configuration (`<root>/.code-rag/config.json`)\n\nPrecedence (low → high): **built-in defaults < config file < environment variables\n(`CODE_RAG_*`) < CLI arguments**. The settings card can edit these whitelisted keys\n(saving writes the file; changes take effect after restarting the Code RAG session):\n\n| Key | Default | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `qdrantUrl` | `http://127.0.0.1:6333` | Qdrant HTTP URL |\n| `ollamaUrl` | `http://127.0.0.1:11434` | Ollama HTTP URL |\n| `embedModel` | `bge-m3` | Embedding model (`ollama pull bge-m3` if missing) |\n| `dimensions` | `1024` | Vector dimensions (bge-m3=1024, nomic-embed-text=768) |\n| `collection` | `code_rag` | Qdrant collection name |\n| `httpPort` | `8756` | Panel HTTP port (auto-probes upward when busy) |\n| `chunkSize` | `150` | Target chunk size in lines |\n| `ignore` | built-in list | Ignore rules, one per line; empty restores defaults |\n\nBuilt-in `ignore` defaults cover `node_modules`, `.git`, `dist`, `build`, `out`,\n`target`, common IDE/build dirs (`.idea`, `.vscode`, `x64`, `obj`,\n`cmake-build-*`, …) and generated artifacts like `*.min.js` (full list in\n`src/config.ts` → `DEFAULTS.ignore`).\n\n## Prerequisites (local, free)\n\nIndexing depends on two local, free components: **Qdrant** (vector store, port 6333)\nand **Ollama** (local embeddings, port 11434). Both must be up before the first index.\n\n### Qdrant (Docker)\n\nOne-shot container:\n\n```bash\ndocker run -d \\\n  --name qdrant \\\n  --restart unless-stopped \\\n  -p 6333:6333 \\\n  -v qdrant_data:/qdrant/storage \\\n  qdrant/qdrant\n```\n\nOr Docker Compose (`docker-compose.yml`):\n\n```yaml\nservices:\n  qdrant:\n    image: qdrant/qdrant\n    ports:\n      - \"6333:6333\"\n    volumes:\n      - qdrant_storage:/qdrant/storage\nvolumes:\n  qdrant_storage:\n```\n\n### Ollama (embedding model)\n\nInstall [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) and pull the default embedding model:\n\n```bash\nollama pull bge-m3\n```\n\n> The settings card's **Re-check** verifies each piece: an unreachable Qdrant or a\n> missing collection, an unreachable Ollama or a missing model — all land in the\n> issue list. Indexing only succeeds once everything is ready.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\ncd code-rag          # the companion repo (Ankali-Aylina/code-rag)\nnpm install && npm run build\nnpm run setup        # generates the Code RAG mode preset + syncs this plugin into the web profile\n```\n\nThen restart DSH and pick **Code RAG mode** for a new session. If the package is\npublished to npm you can also `npm install dsh-code-rag-index-panel` by name.\n\n**Note on applying updates**: `lib/client.js` changes are picked up automatically by\nthe web app's client HMR (no browser refresh needed); `lib/index.js` (host half —\nloopback endpoints, settings-namespace registration) requires a **DSH restart**, and\nthe Settings → Plugins card appears only after that restart registers the namespace.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Pick **Code RAG mode** for a new session in the DSH web mode picker (keep it running — the index server starts with it);\n2. Once the index bar appears above the input, click **Start index** (incremental) or **Full rebuild** — progress shows live (% / files / chunks);\n3. When switching workspaces, ask the model to call `mcp__code_rag__set_root` first (or edit `root` in the settings card);\n4. To tune Qdrant / Ollama / embedding model / chunking, edit and save in the settings card (writes `<root>/.code-rag/config.json`; restart the Code RAG session to apply).\n\n## Self-tests\n\n- Host half: `node scripts/selftest-panel.mjs` (mock ctx, no live server, no writes to user dirs)\n- Client half: `node scripts/selftest-client.mjs` (executes the whole bundle in a mocked browser, verifies slot registration)\n"
    },
